{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CO",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now concerning the collection for the saints, as I have given order to the churches of Galatia, even so do ye.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon the first ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the week, let every one of you lay by him in store, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath prospered him, that there be no collections when I come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when I come, whomsoever ye shall approve by ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " letters, them will I send to bring your liberality to Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if it be proper that I should go also, they shall go with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now I will come to you, when I shall pass through Macedonia: for I am to pass through Macedonia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it may be that I shall abide, and even winter with you, that ye may bring me on my journey whithersoever I go.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I will not see you now by the way; but I trust to tarry a while with you, if the Lord permit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I shall tarry at Ephesus until Pentecost.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a great door and effectual is opened to me, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many adversaries.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now if Timothy come, see that he may be with you without fear: for he worketh the work of the Lord, as I also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let no man therefore despise him: but conduct him forth in peace, that he may come to me: for I look for him with the brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As concerning ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brother Apollos, I greatly desired him to come to you with the brethren: but his will was not at all to come at this time; but he will come when he shall have convenient time.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, acquit yourselves like men, be strong.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let all your things be done with charity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I beseech you, brethren, (ye know the house of Stephanas, that it is the first fruits of Achaia, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they have addicted themselves to the ministry of the saints,)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That ye submit yourselves to such, and to every one that helpeth with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and laboreth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am glad of the coming of Stephanas, and Fortunatus, and Achaicus: for that which was lacking on your part, they have supplied.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have refreshed my spirit and yours: therefore acknowledge ye them that are such.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The churches of Asia salute you. Aquila and Priscilla salute you much in the Lord, with the church that is in their house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the brethren greet you. Greet ye one another with a holy kiss.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The salutation of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Paul with my own hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man loveth not the Lord Jesus Christ, let him be Anathema, Maran-atha.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.16.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.16.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My love ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you all in Christ Jesus. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
